1410.rotationNotes:
Iuno is more than just a buffer. She can also be a main carry.
Iuno's enhanced heavy attack does not cancel her Outro Skill's damage.&nbsp;

Iuno is a character that moves between two modes in her Lunar Cycle, Half Moon and New Moon. When she cast her liberation, the lunar cycle begins. She builds her forte gauge, or Sentience, in the Half Moon mode and when its full, you can activate her New Moon mode, which will put Iuno in the air, to begin dealing massive Aero Damage. Once her concerto is full, Iuno's enhanced heavy attack becomes available. When used, she will grant the entire team the "Full Moon" domain, which will restore allies HP and STA periodically. Additionally, allies who gain a shield in this domain will also gain all DMG amplification.
Iuno's rotation consist of the following: using her liberation which activates her Lunar Cycle, building her forte in Half Moon mode, and when it is full, she will swap to her New Moon mode, and spend her Forte gauge by using Resonance Skill and Basic Attacks. When her concerto is full, she will trigger a heavy attack, and swap to the next character to provide a substantial damage amplification based on the shielding gained by allies.&nbsp;

1411.rotationNotes:
Qiuyuan's Resonance Skill is a deadly counter, so skilled players can use it to negate all damage taken, stagnate the enemy, and follow up with free damage. When outside of combat, he is able to quickly move through the world by holding down his Resonance Skill. &nbsp;

Qiuyuan is a powerful buffer for Echo Skill DMG users, thanks to his outro skill which buffs Echo Skill DMG by 50%. Additionally, he is able to quickly generate Forte, in order to easily trigger his outro skill. He specalizes in Heavy Attack DMG, and many portions of his kit has a unique interaction depending on how filled his Forte Gauge is.
Qiuyuan's Resonance Liberation deals significant Aero Damage, and also buffs the entire team granting them up to 30% Crit DMG. This buff is determined by the excess Crit Rate Qiuyan has over 50%, so its important to have at least 70% Crit Rate on him to max out this buff.
Qiuyuan's rotation is quite simple, when he triggers his Intro Skill, he is able to generate 2/3 gauges of his forte. Once his forte gauge is filled, he will enter "Inkspash of Mind" state. &nbsp;Which allows him to trigger his Thus Spoke The Blade combo, which is 3 consecutive heavy attacks, all considered both Heavy ATK, and Echo Skill DMG.
His rotation consist of Intro Skill &gt; Resonance Liberation &gt; Building one gauge of Forte from basic attacks &gt; Thus Spoke the Blade combo &gt; Outro Skill.&nbsp;

1412.rotationNotes:
Sigrika excels with other Echo Skill users in her team, such as Quiyuan, Phrolova, and Cantarella.&nbsp;
Quickly Fill Sigrika's gauge by using Sigrika's Intro skill, and completing her Basic Attack Combo and Enhanced Heavy attack, then follow up with her Resonance Liberation, and do the same again.&nbsp;
There are 3 types of Enhanced Heavy Attacks, for 3 different situations. Two Trust Runes will cause the enemy to be stagnated, which is great for bosses.&nbsp;
Two Answer Runes will cause nearbyy enemies to be pulled in, which is great for crowd control.&nbsp;
Opposite Runes will deal high damage, making it the ideal choice when the other two options are not required.

Sigrika is a main damage dealing character who empowers herself through her teammates' Echo Skills, allowing her to stagnate enemies while increasing her own damage. Most of her damage is considered Echo Skill Damage.
Sigrika can gain runes by using her Enhanced Heavy Attack after she enters Decipher State. She enters Decipher State after performing Basic Attack Stage 4. During Decipher, her next action generates a Rune slot. When Sigrika has two Rune slots, she can hold Basic Attack to cast an Enhanced Heavy Attack, consuming the Rune slots.
Sigrika is capable of obtaining two different types of runes, Trust and Answer, and each rune is obtained depending on which attack is used in Decipher State. The Trust Rune is gained when she casts her Basic Attack or Dodge Counter during Decipher State. The Answer Rune is gained when she casts her Resonance Skill during Decipher State.
After casting her Enhanced Heavy Attack, she gains 50 points of Full Stop, which caps at 100. After reaching 50 Full Stop, Sigrika's Basic Attack chain begins at Stage 2, allowing her to reach Decipher faster.
In order to speed up this process, Sigrika has two States she can enter, Divergent, which is gained by casting her Resonance Liberation, and Convergent, which is gained by casting her Intro Skill. Convergent takes priority over Divergent. If both are active, Convergent will trigger first. Divergent grants Sigrika an additional OPPOSITE Rune when she obtains a Rune. Convergent grants her the additional SAME type of Rune instead.
When Sigrika's Forte is maxed, she is able to cast her Forte Finisher, "Learn My True Name", dealing Significant Echo Skill Damage.
Sigrika's ideal rotation is to use your other characters first to fully buff the team, then Intro Skill into Sigrika, use her Resonance Liberation, and follow up with her Basic Attack 4 to gain Decipher. You will then either cast a Basic Attack, Dodge Counter, or Resonance Skill to gain your desired Rune, and finish up with her Enhanced Heavy Attack to gain two of the same runes, and gaining 50/100 Full Stop. You can then cast her Basic Attack 4 once more, granting Decipher again, gain your desired rune, and use her Enhanced Heavy Attack to gain your final rune. This will generate 100 points of Full Stop, and she can then casts her Finisher Enhanced Resonance Skill to finish off her rotation.
When Sigrika casts her Outro Skill, she deals huge Aero DMG and gains 2 stacks Encapsulated. When teammates cast an Echo Skill, one Encapsulated stack is consumed and nearby enemies become Stagnated.

